    "label": "Problem 2",
    "statement": "Design a sequential circuit that computes x + 2 in binary: the input numeral arrives one bit per clock tick (least-significant bit first), and the circuit must emit the binary numeral for x + 2 on its output wire, least-significant bit first. Hint: +2 is +1 twice \u2014 you can chain two incrementer blocks, or serially add the constant stream for 2 (a single 1 arriving at the second tick).",
